98 | fences | Staub Field 4 west boundary stone wall with rider fence | - | modern survey; shown on the park 1863 existing-condition map | stated | A stone wall 150 feet long, 1-1.5 feet wide and up to 1.5 feet high, partly collapsed or missing, generally matches the stone wall and fence labelled 'Staub Field No.4 West Boundary Fence and Rider Fence' on the park's 1863 Existing Condition map No. 15; the rider fence atop the wall is no longer present | #s28-31
99 | fences | Stone wall west of the Henry Spangler farm (Wilcox's Brigade stone wall) | - | ~pre-1863 origin; dimensions as surveyed today (modern) | stated | A dry-laid wall of irregular-sized granite boulders (inventory date pre-1863, contributing), east of West Confederate Avenue and west of the H. Spangler Farm, is 1,200 feet long, 3 feet wide and 1 foot high and was erected as a farm field boundary and then incorporated by the armies into battle positions | #s13-17

# --- Reconstructed fences (modern) ---
115 | fences | Reconstructed fences on the Pickett's Charge field | FEN-emmitsburg-road | 2004-2024 reconstruction (modern) | stated | Since 2004 the park has reconstructed thousands of feet of fencing based on historic photographs and maps | Since 2004, the park has reconstructed thousands of feet of fencing based on historic photographs and maps.
115 | fences | Fences standing in the early 2000s | - | ~2004 (National Register documentation) | stated | The 2004 National Register documentation identified several contributing fences in the Pickett's Charge Battlefield area (the Bliss Farm field fence, the boundary fences of the W. J. Althoff, Nicholas Codori and Henry Spangler farms, the boundary road fences of the Joseph Sherfy farm and the Henry Spangler field fence) and called the yard fence of the Francis Althoff farm noncontributing; it is unknown if these were the only fences standing in the early 2000s, and unclear where the fence lines were specifically located | #s6-7
117 | fences | Sherfy Fields 1, 2 and 5 fence type | bld-sherfy-farm | 1863 type uncertain; fence rebuilt 2012 (earlier 1993) | conflict | The sources for the Sherfy field fences disagree: a narrative from Barksdale's Brigade supports post and rail, a Tipton photograph of about 1890 supports post and slab; the park built post and slab in 2012 | The narrative from Barksdale’s Brigade, published 51 years after the battle, >>> last replaced in 1993. | #s11
117 | fences | Sherfy yard picket fences | bld-sherfy-farm | historic imagery (date not given); rebuilt 2011 | stated | In 2011 the park completed the installation of 493 feet of picket fence and four gates along the boundaries of the Sherfy Yards; historic imagery indicates that there were two types of picket fencing at the Sherfy Yards | #s16-17
117 | buildings | Wentz buildings | bld-wentz-farm | modern 2024: buildings gone | stated | The Wentz buildings are no longer extant; the installed fence lines help define the Wentz property and create a definitive edge between the parcels and Wheatfield Road | Installation of these fence lines helped to define the Wentz property since the buildings are no longer extant and to create a definitive edge between the parcels and Wheatfield Road.
117 | fences | Staub Fields 1 and 2 north boundary fences | - | 1999 replacement of 1970s fences (modern) | stated | The worm fence on the north boundary of Staub Field 2 was installed in 1999 as a replacement in kind of a worm fence installed in the 1970s | In 1999, volunteers completed the installation of 440 feet of worm fence >>> worm fence installed in the 1970s.

# --- Chronology (dates of later features) ---
41 | earthworks | Documented 1863 defence works in the Pickett's Charge area | - | 1863-07 | stated | Documented works of 1863: McMillan Woods earthworks and rifle pits, Pender's Division earthworks, Poague's Battalion lunettes and Spangler Woods defence works | CE 1863 Built Documented defenseworks include McMillan Woods >>> Spangler Woods defense works.
41 | buildings | Joseph Sherfy barn (date) | bld-sherfy-farm | !1868 | stated | The inventory's chronology records the building of the Joseph Sherfy barn in 1868 | CE 1868 Built Joseph Sherfy barn is built.
41 | buildings | Nicholas Codori barn (date) | bld-codori-farm | !1884 | stated | The inventory's chronology records the building of the Nicholas Codori barn in 1884 | CE 1884 Built Nicholas Codori barn is built.
42 | avenues | Berdan Avenue | RD-avenues | !1887 | stated | Berdan Avenue was built in 1887 | CE 1887 Built Berdan Avenue is built off of Confederate Avenue in Pitzer Woods.
43 | avenues | West Confederate Avenue | RD-avenues | !1894-1901 | stated | West Confederate Avenue was built in sections from 1894 to 1901 | CE 1894 - 1901 Built West Confederate Avenue is constructed in sections from 1894-1901.
43 | avenues | Birney Avenue | RD-avenues | !1910 | stated | Birney Avenue on the east and south sides of the Peach Orchard was built in 1910 | CE 1910 Built Birney Avenue is built on the east and south sides of the Peach Orchard.
43 | earthworks | Poague's Battalion lunettes | - | ~1901 reconstruction or rehabilitation | stated | Poague's Battalion lunettes were reconstructed or rehabilitated in 1901 by either the GBMA or the War Department | CE 1901 Rehabilitated Poague’s Battalion lunettes are reconstructed or rehabilitated by either the GBMA or the War Department.
44 | monuments | Virginia Monument | - | !1912-1917 | stated | The Virginia Monument was built 1912-1917 | CE 1912 - 1917 Built Virginia Monument is built.
44 | monuments | North Carolina State Monument | - | !1929 | stated | The North Carolina State Monument was erected in 1929 | CE 1929 Memorialized Monument/marker is erected: North Carolina State Monument.
41 | monuments | Earliest monument in the Pickett's Charge area | - | !1884 | stated | The inventory's chronology records the erection in 1884 of the 14th Connecticut Infantry Monument position markers | CE 1884 Memorialized Monument/marker is erected: 14th Connecticut Infantry Monument Position Markers.
42 | monuments | 106th Pennsylvania Infantry Monument | - | !1885-1886 | stated | The 106th Pennsylvania monument and fence were erected in 1885-1886 | CE 1885 - 1886 Memorialized Monument/marker is erected: 106th Pennsylvania Infantry Monument and Fence.
45 | monuments | State monuments on Seminary and Warfield ridges | - | !1963-2000 | stated | Florida (1963), Louisiana (1971), Mississippi (1973), Tennessee (1982), the Longstreet monument (1998) and the 11th Mississippi monument (2000) are all later additions | CE 1963 Memorialized Monument/marker is erected: Florida State Monument. >>> Monument/marker is erected: 11th Mississippi Monument.
45 | orchards | Sherfy Peach Orchard replanting in the 1980s | bld-sherfy-farm,FEN-sherfy-orchard | 1984-1986 replanting (modern) | stated | The Sherfy Peach Orchard was replanted in the mid-1980s | CE 1984 - 1986 Planted In the mid-1980s the Sherfy Peach Orchard is replanted.

